course: dictionary
lesson: 6046
title: One word, many meanings: mend
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mend can be a verb (a doing word) or a noun (a naming word). Its main meaning is to repair something that is broken, torn or not working. In «Rat and Mole were painting and varnishing, mending paddles», the word means they were fixing the paddles so the boats would work again.
explain: Mend can also mean to get better after an illness or injury, so bones mend after a break. The words around mend give you the clue. A torn shirt or a broken toy means repair. A hurt leg or a sick person means heal.
explain: Mend can also mean to make a situation or friendship better. «Trust is like a glass bridge... but mending it takes many careful days» uses mending for rebuilding trust after it has been broken. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: «Mend» means to repair something broken, torn or not working.
fact: «Mend» can mean to heal, as bones do after a break.
fact: «Mend a friendship» means to make things better after a quarrel.
fact: «On the mend» means getting better after an illness or injury.
fact: Kintsugi is a Japanese art of mending broken pottery with gold, so the repaired cracks are shown and admired.
exercise: «Rat and Mole were painting and varnishing, mending paddles, repairing cushions.» In this sentence, what does mending mean? | Sending a letter | *Repairing something that is broken | Feeling better after an illness | Making friends again
exercise: Mum says, «Dad is on the mend after his operation.» What does on the mend mean? | *Getting better after an illness | Broken into pieces | Lost and cannot be found | Busy with a hobby
exercise: «Trust is like a glass bridge: mending it takes many careful days.» What does mending trust mean? | Ignoring the problem and hoping it goes away | Painting the bridge red | Buying a new glass bridge | *Making a broken trust better again
test: «There they find Taffy making daisy-chains and Tegumai happily spearing small carp with his mended spear.» What does mended mean in «his mended spear»? | Brand new from the shop | Lost in the river | Broken and useless | *Repaired so it works again
test: Which sentence uses mend as a noun, a naming word? | *The shirt has a neat mend at the elbow. | We mend fences every single week. | She will mend slowly when she rests. | I will mend my bike after school.
exam: Ella thinks mend only means sewing clothes. Which answer shows she is wrong? | *Mend can also mean to heal, or to make a friendship better | Mend only ever means sewing | Mend only means to paint a boat | Mend means to break things on purpose
